========================================================================================================
(1)  CORRECTNESS:  does the design encoding reproduce the gradient?
========================================================================================================
  Scored against exact parameter-shift at the same theta. R = 0.45,
  16384 shots per circuit, 3 seeds, layered blocks for both.

    N   M  encoding  reg qubits  blocks  cos vs exact
  ---------------------------------------------------
    4  24    onehot           4       6        0.9810
    4  24    design           4       6        0.9860
  ...................................................
    6  36    onehot           6       6        0.9796
    6  36    design           4       6        0.9729
  ...................................................

  The two encodings must land on the same cosine. A gap means the sign
  convention is wrong, and a wrong sign is silent rather than loud.

========================================================================================================
(2)  WHAT IT UNLOCKS:  all M parameters in ONE block
========================================================================================================
  block_mode='global' sets L = 1, so circuits per gradient fall from G*L to
  G. Register need under one-hot is M qubits; under the design it is
  ceil(log2(M+1)) + 1.

  Compared at MATCHED TOTAL SHOTS. Global runs 6x fewer circuits, so it gets
  6x the shots on each; comparing at equal shots-per-circuit would hand
  layered six times the budget and mean nothing.

    N   M            config   reg  circuits  shots/circ   T total  cos vs exact
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    4  24onehot/layered/marginal     4        18       16384    294912        0.9810
    4  24design/global/marginal     6         3       98304    294912        0.7761
    4  24 design/global/wls     6         3       98304    294912        0.7766
  ..................................................................................
    6  36onehot/layered/marginal     6        18       16384    294912        0.9796
    6  36design/global/marginal     7         3       98304    294912        0.8340
    6  36 design/global/wls     7         3       98304    294912        0.8339
  ..................................................................................

  One-hot at N=6 would need 36 register qubits plus 6 system, which is not
  simulable here; that row exists only because of the encoding.

========================================================================================================
(2b) IS THE GLOBAL-BLOCK DEFICIT BIAS, AND IS R THE CAUSE?
========================================================================================================
  A block of n parameters displaces the state by ~sqrt(n)*R, so the radius
  that is right for a 6-parameter block over-displaces a 36-parameter one by
  about 2.4x and the linearisation E ~ E0 + R sum_j g_j sigma_j degrades.
  WLS cannot help with that: it removes cross terms, which is VARIANCE, and
  this would be BIAS. If sweeping R recovers the accuracy, the global deficit
  is a radius that was never re-tuned for the wider block, not a property of
  wide blocks. If it does not, wide blocks genuinely cost accuracy.

    N       R  cos global  cos layered @ R=0.45
  ---------------------------------------------
    4    0.05      0.9252                0.9810
    4    0.10      0.9823                0.9810
    4    0.18      0.9775                0.9810
    4    0.30      0.9322                0.9810
    4    0.45      0.7761                0.9810
  .............................................
    6    0.05      0.8650                0.9796
    6    0.10      0.9525                0.9796
    6    0.18      0.9778                0.9796
    6    0.30      0.9549                0.9796
    6    0.45      0.8340                0.9796
  .............................................

========================================================================================================
(3)  WHAT IT COSTS:  transpiled depth and two-qubit gates per GRADIENT
========================================================================================================
  Common hardware basis ['rz', 'sx', 'x', 'cx'], so neither arm is flattered by a
  simulator basis that keeps cry as one gate.

    N                config  circuits  depth/circ   2q/circ  2q per gradient
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    4        onehot/layered        18          32        14              252
    4        design/layered        18          53        22              396
    4         design/global         3         157        82              246
  .........................................................................
    6        onehot/layered        18          34        22              396
    6        design/layered        18          69        32              576
    6         design/global         3         229       124              372
  .........................................................................

  '2q per gradient' is the number that matters: circuits times two-qubit
  gates each. The design trades a control qubit per parameter for parity
  CNOTs, so per circuit it should cost MORE, and only wins if the circuit
  count falls faster than the per-circuit cost rises.
